{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789936640,"nonce":"58fjyEw0bbIR6Li9h+HPC9iYI1g=","title":"drop_insert: deciding which phis own their values is quadratic in the function","message":"`release_owned_phis` starts with every phi as a candidate and, each\nround, asks per candidate and per incoming which phis read a value\n(a scan of every block), what is derived from it (rebuilding the use\nindex each time) and whether all its uses borrow (a scan of every\ninstruction). Rounds repeat until no candidate drops out.\n\nOn a 1000-block function with a thousand phis (a Lua chunk with forty\nmethod-call sites, or nbody's advance) the pass took 200 ms per body,\npaid again for every tier that compiles the function, and dominated the\nprogram's start.\n\nFix: candidates are only phis whose type may be storage; the phis\nreading each value, each value's defining block, its derived set and\nwhether its uses borrow are indexed once for the function, and the\nborrow check walks only the instructions that use a derived value.","files":null}]}